#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133479 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133916 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40486856-137f-55c4-8464-f99e7e1c659f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Mixed Integral"}] :question/id #uuid "1b09be02-1515-5277-bac6-9289b9dbe371" :question/math-academy-id "e-11506" :question/problem "Evaluate the mixed integral \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_D \\left[ \\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}} 2y\\: \\mathrm{d}y \\right ]  \\mathrm{d}A,\n$$\n\ngiven that $D$ is the region in the $xz$-plane bounded by the lines $z=0,$ $x= 1$ and the line $z =x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}2y\\,dy]dA & ={∬}_{D}[{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=\\sqrt{x}}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate this double integral, we plot $D$ as a type I plane region in the $xz$-plane.\n\n![](images/1d/1d102b63c3deb8121ea88cdc994b9410cf28f9c3bb29abc5ea4a14d7e1e7c389.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, to evaluate our double integral as a repeated integral over this region, we integrate with respect to $z$ and then with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}x\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x[z]_{z=0}^{z=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133480 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133917 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf29db1b-f47b-53de-b31d-e4da1d0a9e5f" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Triple Integral as a Mixed or Repeated Integral"}] :question/id #uuid "216b16aa-d279-519e-a749-b9fd5517a6db" :question/math-academy-id "e-11507" :question/problem "Find the missing limits in the repeated integral below\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iiint \\limits_{R} f(x,y,z) \\: \\textrm{d}V \n= \n\\int_{\\ast}^{\\ast} \n\\int_{\\ast}^{\\ast} \n\\int_{\\ast}^{\\ast} \nf(x,y,z) \\: \\mathrm{d}y \\: \\mathrm{d}z \\: \\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is the type III region defined as\n\n$$\nR=\\left\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: -3 \\leq x \\leq 3, \\: x \\leq z \\leq 2x+2, \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq z+xz \\right\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A type III region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR = \\big\\{ (x,y,z)  \\: : \\: (x,z) \\in D, \\: u_1(x,z) \\leq y \\leq u_2(x,z) \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type III region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/06/0603bed12c6af74e46544d8bebc52362aed95a9a5ad7418ea4faaf228f3b5241.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type III region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\iiint\\limits_{R} f(x,y,z)\\,\\textrm d V = \\iint\\limits_{D} \\left[\\int_{u_1(x,z)}^{u_2(x,z)} f(x,y,z)\\,\\textrm d y \\right] \\,\\textrm d A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nu_1(x,z) = 0, \\qquad u_2(x,z)  = z+xz.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iiint \\limits_{S} f(x,y,z) \\: \\textrm{d}V \n= \n\\iint\\limits_{D} \\left[ \\int_{0}^{z+xz} f(x,y,z) \\: \\mathrm{d}y \\right] \\mathrm{d}A.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD =\\left\\{ (x,z) \\: : \\: -3 \\leq x \\leq 3, \\: x \\leq z \\leq 2x+2 \\right\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by expressing the double integral over $D$ as a repeated integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{z+xz}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA & ={\\int }_{-3}^{3}{\\int }_{x}^{2x+2}[{\\int }_{0}^{z+xz}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dz\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{3}{\\int }_{x}^{2x+2}{\\int }_{0}^{z+xz}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133483 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133923 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4693bb81-f299-50fa-9cbd-3a5bb1c90da9" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Over a Type III Region"}] :question/id #uuid "72b1ac41-be39-5a51-bc0c-738d36cdb81b" :question/math-academy-id "e-12378" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iiint\\limits_R 8xy  \\: \\mathrm{d}V\n$$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR = \\left\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: (x,z) \\in D, \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq \\sqrt x \\right\\},\n$$\n\nand $D$ is the finite region in $xz$-plane enclosed between the $x$-axis, the line $x=1,$ and the line $z=x$ in the first quadrant." :question/worked-solution "Writing down our triple integral as a mixed integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iiint \\limits_{R} 8xy \\, \\textrm{d}V\n=\n\\iint\\limits_D \\left[ \\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}} 8xy\\: \\mathrm{d}y \\right ]  \\mathrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}8xy\\,dy]dA & ={∬}_{D}4x[{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=\\sqrt{x}}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}4x(x-0)\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}4{x}^{2}\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now evaluate this double integral over the region $D$ in the $xz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](images/1d/1d102b63c3deb8121ea88cdc994b9410cf28f9c3bb29abc5ea4a14d7e1e7c389.png)\n\nWe can evaluate our double integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}4{x}^{2}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}4{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4{x}^{2}[z]_{z=0}^{z=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4{x}^{2}(x-0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & ={1}^{4}-0 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133485 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133925 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1889f67-327c-5e6e-b646-5bd58a244778" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing and Evaluating Triple Integrals Over Type III Regions From Diagrams"}] :question/id #uuid "21fdb746-8831-5b97-acf0-5a14a2e34980" :question/math-academy-id "e-12400" :question/problem "![](images/b0/b0817c04ee57a8352f8f56a4c232668d415c1573e37a81729752d65c0fb9e1c1.png)\n\n \n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n$\\displaystyle \\iiint\\limits_R 36z^2  \\: \\mathrm{d}V$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the right one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](images/05/0584c95ae22135288f08fc8d0ef472aae867eccecf958c65e82eb311da69a1ae.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type III region\n\n$$\nR = \\big\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: (x,z) \\in D, \\:\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 5-x-z \\big\\},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,z) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq z \\leq 1 \\big\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/36/365451aa395e91cee59199b048ed59ce1fba2ee8ee569fc460ef8fe9bf3bcdfd.png)\n\nHence, the type III representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR = \\big\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq z \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 5-x-z \\big\\}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iiint \\limits_{R} 36z^2 \\: \\textrm{d}V \n= \n\\int_{0}^{1} \\int_{0}^{1} \\int_{0}^{5-x-z} 36z^2 \\: \\mathrm{d}y \\: \\mathrm{d}z \\: \\mathrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{5-x-z}36{z}^{2}\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{5-x-z}36{z}^{2}\\,dy]dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}36{z}^{2}[y]_{y=0}^{y=5-x-z}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}36{z}^{2}(5-x-z)\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(180{z}^{2}-36x{z}^{2}-36{z}^{3})\\,dz\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(180{z}^{2}-36x{z}^{2}-36{z}^{3})\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}(180{z}^{2}-36x{z}^{2}-36{z}^{3})\\,dz]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[60{z}^{3}-12x{z}^{3}-9{z}^{4}]_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(51-12x)\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(51-12x)\\,dx & =[51x-6{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(51(1)-6(1)^{2})-0 \\\\  & =45\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281307 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133917 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf29db1b-f47b-53de-b31d-e4da1d0a9e5f" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Triple Integral as a Mixed or Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fa5bdff-7005-5ec5-8d80-f8b856c23017" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-z}^{{x}^{2}+z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279010} {:answer/id #uuid "6597255a-aab0-55f2-9ed7-2df3b0c5bd5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-z}^{{x}^{2}+z}[{∬}_{D}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279514} {:answer/id #uuid "7fe1f465-25bf-5d62-ae2b-845bc56fcc26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}+z}^{-z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dz" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279740} {:answer/id #uuid "c9d00fb8-2293-5455-a322-7d10609e79d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}+z}^{-z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280358} {:answer/id #uuid "e0d44e8b-e4d8-593a-a817-7e8b04fb3f94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-z}^{{x}^{2}+z}f(x,y,z)\\,dz]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280583}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2fa5bdff-7005-5ec5-8d80-f8b856c23017" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-z}^{{x}^{2}+z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279010} :answer-field/id #uuid "9575c3e7-857c-5f96-ad84-b47a94df34c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281102}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2f13673d-47ba-5a25-8690-9d3a570aad64" :question/math-academy-id "q-161722" :question/problem "Consider the type III region $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,-z\\le y\\le {x}^{2}+z},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is some finite region in the $xz$-plane. Then,\n\n$$\n{∭}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A type III region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(x,z)\\le y\\le {u}_{2}(x,z)}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type III region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/06/0603bed12c6af74e46544d8bebc52362aed95a9a5ad7418ea4faaf228f3b5241.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type III region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,z)}^{{u}_{2}(x,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(x,z)=-z,\\,{u}_{2}(x,z)={x}^{2}+z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-z}^{{x}^{2}+z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281312 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133916 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40486856-137f-55c4-8464-f99e7e1c659f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Mixed Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "361bfe9b-b263-5de7-93b7-f4db26264c8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279065} {:answer/id #uuid "74283afe-9e20-5de9-a9ee-f485a91d9c20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279640} {:answer/id #uuid "78aca257-927d-598a-a519-e0eb2ba39a6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279666} {:answer/id #uuid "7d2dbf0f-2ebb-5bee-a881-105fa780856d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279710} {:answer/id #uuid "9566a15c-dee3-5f61-8f42-b9b8f56fd259" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279920}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9566a15c-dee3-5f61-8f42-b9b8f56fd259" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279920} :answer-field/id #uuid "2eb2ba9a-f03f-55df-8fb0-cec85d841b52" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280919}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4b555d9f-d5f9-558f-a244-86b96b18ac88" :question/math-academy-id "q-161733" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}4zy\\,dy]dA,\n$$\n\nEvaluate the repeated integral above given that $D$ is a region in the $xz$-plane bounded by the lines $z=0,$ $x=2$ and the line $z-x=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}4zy\\,dy]dA & ={∬}_{D}2z[{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=\\sqrt{x}}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2zx\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate this double integral, we plot $D$ as a type I plane region in the $xz$-plane.\n\n![](images/b7/b748f589d7fa773444fc45bdbd1d94a5424bb81c40851f0f0f2542a4f66c0c8d.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, to evaluate our double integral as a repeated integral over this region, we integrate with respect to $z$ and then with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2zx\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}2zx\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x[{z}^{2}]_{z=0}^{z=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =4-0 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281313 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133923 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4693bb81-f299-50fa-9cbd-3a5bb1c90da9" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Over a Type III Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "415161dd-cdcb-5425-acb1-938cd55cb558" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279174} {:answer/id #uuid "7626f571-253c-5ce7-9602-4e73e0d03ae4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279646} {:answer/id #uuid "c7929a24-2bd5-5143-a65f-50417cb26bc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280341} {:answer/id #uuid "d47896b0-3c68-5df1-9e8f-025e32352d5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280465} {:answer/id #uuid "f99e0a64-1e5b-5066-84d8-97275f14d7c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "415161dd-cdcb-5425-acb1-938cd55cb558" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279174} :answer-field/id #uuid "af73b320-686f-5899-8f90-0fd38634d25e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281136}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ff27e038-e43c-5a90-b151-748220a86ed2" :question/math-academy-id "q-161735" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}12y\\,dV\n$$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}},\n$$\n\nand $D$ is a finite region in $xz$-plane enclosed between the $x$-axis, the line $x=1,$ and the line $z=x$ in the first quadrant." :question/worked-solution "Writing down our triple integral as a mixed integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}12y\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}12y\\,dy]dA.\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}12y\\,dy]dA & ={∬}_{D}6[{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=\\sqrt{x}}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}6x\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe must now evaluate this double integral over the region $D$ in the $xz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](images/1d/1d102b63c3deb8121ea88cdc994b9410cf28f9c3bb29abc5ea4a14d7e1e7c389.png)\n\n \n\nWe can evaluate our double integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}6x\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}6x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6x[z]_{z=0}^{z=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[2{x}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281317 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133923 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4693bb81-f299-50fa-9cbd-3a5bb1c90da9" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Over a Type III Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e0673f9-49be-5b89-b056-38db50720c36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278995} {:answer/id #uuid "717da108-6fee-53dd-a64c-56bda00fabfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279621} {:answer/id #uuid "8d059927-b69b-5ea3-a1c9-5cdbd981ac25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279849} {:answer/id #uuid "a5bbe5f5-1301-5da1-a4a3-b42afc64de96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280061} {:answer/id #uuid "d2b7b408-79ac-599e-9d52-7731e5ecb06f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5bbe5f5-1301-5da1-a4a3-b42afc64de96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280061} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c28af51-d8e7-53ee-b355-cdf9be35b210" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281060}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f9e6176f-e02b-5e64-8d69-eb13369492af" :question/math-academy-id "q-161751" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}20y\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is the type III region given by \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le 1-{x}^{2},\\,0\\le y\\le 1-x}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2x\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}20y\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}20y\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}[{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}20y\\,dy]dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}[10{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=1-x}dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}10(1-x)^{2}\\,dz\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}10(1-x)^{2}\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}10(1-x)^{2}\\,dz]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}10(1-x)^{2}[z]_{z=0}^{z=1-{x}^{2}}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}10(1-x)^{2}(1-{x}^{2})dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}10(1-2x+2{x}^{3}-{x}^{4})\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}10(1-2x+2{x}^{3}-{x}^{4})\\,dx & ={[10(x-{x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5})]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281358 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133925 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1889f67-327c-5e6e-b646-5bd58a244778" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing and Evaluating Triple Integrals Over Type III Regions From Diagrams"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d48cc3d-ead9-593f-915c-d3aaa480ed03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278715} {:answer/id #uuid "3e139408-c514-52b7-89df-e2b959afe3df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279139} {:answer/id #uuid "5e531d96-5cc8-51fb-a104-07e94c5bec18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279456} {:answer/id #uuid "c6bcddbb-ebc8-5c7b-ad03-f16d13624465" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280333} {:answer/id #uuid "cc2fc060-126f-54c6-ba8f-9f107326389f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280384}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d48cc3d-ead9-593f-915c-d3aaa480ed03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278715} :answer-field/id #uuid "544d160b-e29b-59aa-9938-64c90c8cfe69" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280972}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2dd43989-4160-5cb0-b938-4fe05b8b6278" :question/math-academy-id "q-161853" :question/problem "![](images/a1/a1e4a1e39c85a037f3f4f49910b651300363ef34bee969464f5e711aa00986e3.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}4{x}^{2}z\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the right one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](images/91/9165163be9ce95e7165f04d26e6ce8080699ab4d477eba3f804c849fdf1fb679.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type III region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 4-z},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/ca/ca74bf149c1371fe9f1622586d9eb92fe180a9c9bb6a0c53d16f538b3c55f4a4.png)\n\nHence, the type III representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 4-z}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}4{x}^{2}z\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4-z}4{x}^{2}z\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4-z}4{x}^{2}z\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{4-z}4{x}^{2}z\\,dy]dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}4{x}^{2}z[y]_{y=0}^{y=4-z}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}4{x}^{2}z(4-z)\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(16{x}^{2}z-4{x}^{2}{z}^{2})\\,dz\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(16{x}^{2}z-4{x}^{2}{z}^{2})\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}(16{x}^{2}z-4{x}^{2}{z}^{2})\\,dz]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[8{x}^{2}{z}^{2}-\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{2}{z}^{3}]_{z=0}^{z=3}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}36{x}^{2}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}36{x}^{2}\\,dx & ={[12{x}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(12-0) \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134287 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133916 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40486856-137f-55c4-8464-f99e7e1c659f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Mixed Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26371e7c-d4aa-5cd0-a363-95439d905659" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324279} {:answer/id #uuid "4d153674-baf0-565f-a0eb-dec9cc52f8a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324608} {:answer/id #uuid "9a3d06d0-0635-568c-b9ca-dac6fef15963" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325283} {:answer/id #uuid "9b0a8c83-7180-5d2f-946a-f9b34a2d351d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325291} {:answer/id #uuid "d4882293-69d6-5858-b2d4-78dc60ebf4d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325820}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a3d06d0-0635-568c-b9ca-dac6fef15963" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325283} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6c48fd4-9172-51c8-a0ec-c24aea7453e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326519}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e6d26c08-ceec-5b48-a4a3-f3df87eec565" :question/math-academy-id "q-40403" :question/problem "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}2xyz\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\ngiven that the region $D$ in the $xz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{4-2z},\\,0\\le z\\le 2}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}2xyz\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}xz[{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{3}z\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type II region in the $xz$-plane.\nTherefore, to evaluate our double integral as a repeated integral over this region, we integrate with respect to $x$ and then with respect to $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{x}^{3}z\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-2z}}{x}^{3}z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}z[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-2z}}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}z{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{4-2z}}\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{4}(4-2z)^{2}z\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}4z-4{z}^{2}+{z}^{3}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={[2{z}^{2}-\\frac{4}{3}{z}^{3}+\\frac{1}{4}{z}^{4}]}_{z=0}^{z=2} \\\\  & =(8-\\frac{32}{3}+4)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134293 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133917 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf29db1b-f47b-53de-b31d-e4da1d0a9e5f" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Triple Integral as a Mixed or Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e2c97d4-b434-5053-9663-fa52d98d5684" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324100} {:answer/id #uuid "4b299549-5cb0-56d7-9c33-9a26cc8d61bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324580} {:answer/id #uuid "95a97664-7cb4-546a-9467-1efee24db627" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325246} {:answer/id #uuid "9ecaa195-92d6-5644-a84f-02c83f6bf09c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325317} {:answer/id #uuid "b67b4bdb-21a2-5cc7-a126-ffb05118dd40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b67b4bdb-21a2-5cc7-a126-ffb05118dd40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325537} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d2a35f2-61ae-55fb-8f9b-a4bff3e74ef2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326502}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f9f2f2a5-47b5-5a66-9153-5085ab9c95cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-40503" :question/problem "$$\n{∭}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx\n$$\n\nThe triple integral above is defined over the type III region given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,-1\\le z\\le 2x+1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1+x+z}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "A type III region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(x,z)\\le y\\le {u}_{2}(x,z)}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type III region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/06/0603bed12c6af74e46544d8bebc52362aed95a9a5ad7418ea4faaf228f3b5241.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type III region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,z)}^{{u}_{2}(x,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(x,z)=0,\\,{u}_{2}(x,z)=1+x+z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{1+x+z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,-1\\le z\\le 2x+1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by expressing the double integral over $D$ as a repeated integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{1+x+z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2x+1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1+x+z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dz\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{2x+1}{\\int }_{0}^{1+x+z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b=(-1)+(2x+1)=2x.\n$$"}]}
